    "problem_statement": "### Issue: TypeError when unpickling abstract base classes\n\n#### Description\n\nEncountering a `TypeError` when attempting to unpickle abstract base classes (ABCs) that have been registered with subclasses. This issue seems to arise when using `cloudpickle` to serialize and deserialize classes that utilize the `abc` module for defining abstract methods and properties.\n\n#### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Define an abstract base class using `abc.ABC` with abstract methods, class methods, static methods, and properties.\n2. Register a concrete subclass with the abstract base class.\n3. Serialize the abstract base class using `cloudpickle.dumps`.\n4. Deserialize the class using `cloudpickle.loads`.\n5. Attempt to instantiate the deserialized abstract base class or check subclass relationships.\n\n#### Example Code\n\n```python\nimport abc\nimport cloudpickle\n\nclass AbstractClass(abc.ABC):\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def some_method(self):\n        pass\n\n    @classmethod\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def some_classmethod(cls):\n        pass\n\n    @staticmethod\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def some_staticmethod():\n        pass\n\n    @property\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def some_property(self):\n        pass\n\nclass ConcreteClass(AbstractClass):\n    def some_method(self):\n        return 'it works!'\n\n    @classmethod\n    def some_classmethod(cls):\n        return 'it works!'\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def some_staticmethod():\n        return 'it works!'\n\n    @property\n    def some_property(self):\n        return 'it works!'\n\nAbstractClass.register(tuple)\n\n# Serialize and deserialize\ns = cloudpickle.dumps(AbstractClass)\ndepickled_base = cloudpickle.loads(s)\n\n# This raises a TypeError\nassert issubclass(tuple, depickled_base)\n```\n\n#### Actual Outcome\n\nA `TypeError` is raised when attempting to check subclass relationships or instantiate the deserialized abstract base class.\n\n#### Expected Outcome\n\nThe deserialized abstract base class should maintain its subclass relationships and allow instantiation of concrete subclasses without raising a `TypeError`.\n\n#### Additional Information\n\nThis issue affects the ability to use `cloudpickle` for serializing and deserializing classes that rely on the `abc` module for abstract method definitions. The problem seems to be related to how the abstract methods and properties are handled during the unpickling process."
  },
